Local patch (Obcell): backport of srsRAN_4G commit 76a1131d1d0a ("fix issues detected during
gcc 13.2.0 compilation", Piotr Gawlowicz, 2024-04-25), which no release tag contains yet.
Only the srsue hunk; the srsenb header it also touches doesn't exist in release_23_11.

phy_common::reset_measurements(cc_idx >= SRSRAN_MAX_CARRIERS) resets every carrier and then
fell through to write index cc_idx of the per-carrier arrays: an out-of-bounds write on every
phy_common::reset(). GCC 13 (Ubuntu 24.04) stops the build on it with -Werror=array-bounds.

diff --git a/srsue/src/phy/phy_common.cc b/srsue/src/phy/phy_common.cc
index 58ad6a5ca0f..d87949730c7 100644
--- a/srsue/src/phy/phy_common.cc
+++ b/srsue/src/phy/phy_common.cc
@@ -646,6 +646,7 @@ void phy_common::reset_measurements(uint32_t cc_idx)
     for (uint32_t cc = 0; cc < SRSRAN_MAX_CARRIERS; cc++) {
       reset_measurements(cc);
     }
+    return;
   }
 
   // Default all metrics to NAN to prevent providing invalid information on traces and other layers
